  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser, so nothing has been seen rendering yet.\n\n- **Soldier:** `/assets/soldier.glb` is loaded through `defineModelAssets` at a height of 1.8 and plays `Walk` in a loop. I copied the sha256 and clip list from the docs recipe for this fixture without checking them against the actual file.\n- **Path:** each frame the soldier is placed on the radius-4 circle around the origin. Its yaw is `angle + π/2`, so it faces the direction of travel. This assumes the model faces +Z; if it walks backwards, change `FACING_OFFSET` to `Math.PI`.\n- **Gait keys:** `r` switches to `Run` and `w` back to `Walk`, using `play(..., { crossFade: 0.4 })`. Ground speed eases between 1.5 m/s (walk) and 3.6 m/s (run) over about the same time as the crossfade.\n- **Scene:** a 20×20 ground plane, a neutral environment, a hemisphere light, and a shadow-casting directional light. The fixed perspective camera at `[0, 8.5, 10.5]` looks at the origin, so the whole circle stays in frame.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the second frame callback after `app.ready()` resolves.\n\nI tried a ring marker for the path and removed it, because I couldn't confirm how the ring primitive sizes itself. The ground has no marking of the circle.\n\n",
